          {
            "id": 2839518,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "Part four. You will hear a student on a fashion design course giving a talk about the history of pockets. First, you have some time to look at questions 31 to 40. Now listen carefully and answer questions 31 to 40.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2839519,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Part four.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 2.32,
                  "from": 1.12,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 0"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839522,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "You will hear a student on a fashion design course giving a talk about the history of pockets.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 8.799999,
                  "from": 2.8,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 0"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839541,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "First, you have some time to look at questions 31 to 40.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 13.84,
                  "from": 9.76,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 0"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839554,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Now listen carefully and answer questions 31 to 40.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 68.67,
                  "from": 64.189995,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 0"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2839564,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "Good morning. Now we've been asked to choose an aspect of European clothing or fashion and to talk about its development over time. I decided to focus on a rather small area of clothing, and that's pockets. I chose pockets for two reasons, really. We all have them in jeans, jackets, coats, for example, and even though we often carry bags or briefcases as well, nothing is quite as convenient as being able to pop your phone or credit card into your pocket.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2839565,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Good morning.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 73.375,
                  "from": 72.415,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839568,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Now we've been asked to choose an aspect of European clothing or fashion and to talk about its development over time.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 81.615,
                  "from": 73.854996,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839590,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "I decided to focus on a rather small area of clothing, and that's pockets.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 87.534996,
                  "from": 82.335,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839605,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "I chose pockets for two reasons, really.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 91.43,
                  "from": 88.55,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839613,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "We all have them in jeans, jackets, coats, for example, and even though we often carry bags or briefcases as well, nothing is quite as convenient as being able to pop your phone or credit card into your pocket.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 107.685,
                  "from": 91.990005,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2839653,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "Yet, I suspect that other than that, people don't really think about pockets too much, and they're rather overlooked as a fashion item. It's certainly very interesting to go back in time and see how pockets developed for men and women. In the eighteenth century, fashions were quite different from the way they are now, and pockets were too. If we think about male fashion first, that was the time when suits became popular. Trousers were knee length only and referred to as breeches.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2839654,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Yet, I suspect that other than that, people don't really think about pockets too much, and they're rather overlooked as a fashion item.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 117.48,
                  "from": 108.485,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839678,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "It's certainly very interesting to go back in time and see how pockets developed for men and women.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 125.08,
                  "from": 118.520004,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839697,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "In the eighteenth century, fashions were quite different from the way they are now, and pockets were too.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 132.485,
                  "from": 125.64,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839716,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "If we think about male fashion first, that was the time when suits became popular.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 140.085,
                  "from": 133.285,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839732,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Trousers were knee length only and referred to as breeches.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 146.07,
                  "from": 141.11,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2839743,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "The waistcoats were short, and the jackets were long. But all three garments were lined with material, and pockets were sewn into this cloth by whichever tailor the customer used. The wearer could then carry small objects such as pencils or coins on their person and reach them through a gap in the lining. Coat pockets became increasingly decorative on the outside for men who wanted to look stylish, but they were often larger but plainer if the wearer was someone with a profession who needed to carry medical instruments a doctor or physician, for example. The development of women's pockets was a little different.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2839744,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "The waistcoats were short, and the jackets were long.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 150.23,
                  "from": 146.62999,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839754,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "But all three garments were lined with material, and pockets were sewn into this cloth by whichever tailor the customer used.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 159.725,
                  "from": 150.79,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839776,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "The wearer could then carry small objects such as pencils or coins on their person and reach them through a gap in the lining.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 169.325,
                  "from": 160.765,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839801,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Coat pockets became increasingly decorative on the outside for men who wanted to look stylish, but they were often larger but plainer if the wearer was someone with a profession who needed to carry medical instruments a doctor or physician, for example.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 189.02501,
                  "from": 170.68001,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839844,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "The development of women's pockets was a little different.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 198.065,
                  "from": 194.065,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2839854,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "For one thing, they weren't nearly as visible or as easy to reach as men's. In the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries, women carried numerous possessions on their person, and some of these could be worth a lot of money. Women were more vulnerable to theft, and wealthy women, in particular, worried constantly about pickpockets. So what they did was to have a pair of pockets made that were tied together with string. The pockets were made of fabric, which might be recycled cloth if the wearer had little money, or something more expensive, such as linen, sometimes featuring very delicate embroidery.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2839855,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "For one thing, they weren't nearly as visible or as easy to reach as men's.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 204.35,
                  "from": 199.07,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839871,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "In the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries, women carried numerous possessions on their person, and some of these could be worth a lot of money.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 215.07501,
                  "from": 205.23001,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839896,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Women were more vulnerable to theft, and wealthy women, in particular, worried constantly about pickpockets.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 223.63501,
                  "from": 216.195,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839912,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "So what they did was to have a pair of pockets made that were tied together with string.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 230.84001,
                  "from": 224.92,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839931,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "The pockets were made of fabric, which might be recycled cloth if the wearer had little money, or something more expensive, such as linen, sometimes featuring very delicate embroidery.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 244.655,
                  "from": 231.56,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2839961,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "Women tied the pockets around their waist so that they hung beneath their clothes. Remember, skirts were long then, and there was plenty of room to hide a whole range of small possessions between the layers of petticoats that were commonly worn. They would have an opening in the folds of their skirts, through which they could reach whatever they needed, like their perfume. Working women, of course, also needed to carry around items that they might use for whatever job or trade they were involved in, but their pairs of pockets still remained on the inside of their clothing. They just got bigger or longer, sometimes reaching down to their knees.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2839962,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Women tied the pockets around their waist so that they hung beneath their clothes.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 250.655,
                  "from": 245.69499,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2839977,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Remember, skirts were long then, and there was plenty of room to hide a whole range of small possessions between the layers of petticoats that were commonly worn.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 261.64,
                  "from": 251.64,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2840006,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "They would have an opening in the folds of their skirts, through which they could reach whatever they needed, like their perfume.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 270.035,
                  "from": 262.52,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2840029,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Working women, of course, also needed to carry around items that they might use for whatever job or trade they were involved in, but their pairs of pockets still remained on the inside of their clothing.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 284.52002,
                  "from": 271.155,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2840066,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "They just got bigger or longer, sometimes reaching down to their knees.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 290.2,
                  "from": 285.08,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2840079,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "So the tie on pockets went well into the nineteenth century and only changed when fashion altered towards the end of that period. That's when dresses became tighter and less bulky, and the pairs of pockets became very noticeable. They stood out too much and detracted from the woman's image. Women who had been used to carrying around a range of personal possessions and still wanted to needed somewhere to carry these items about their person. That was when small bags, or pouches as they were known, came into fashion, and, of course, they inevitably led onto the handbag of more modern times, particularly when fashion removed pockets altogether.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2840080,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "So the tie on pockets went well into the nineteenth century and only changed when fashion altered towards the end of that period.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 301.905,
                  "from": 291.98502,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2840104,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "That's when dresses became tighter and less bulky, and the pairs of pockets became very noticeable.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 309.62003,
                  "from": 302.705,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2840121,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "They stood out too much and detracted from the woman's image.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 314.18002,
                  "from": 310.18002,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2840133,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Women who had been used to carrying around a range of personal possessions and still wanted to needed somewhere to carry these items about their person.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 325.005,
                  "from": 315.06,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2840160,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "That was when small bags, or pouches as they were known, came into fashion, and, of course, they inevitably led onto the handbag of more modern times, particularly when fashion removed pockets altogether.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 342.42,
                  "from": 325.965,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
