            "content": "<h2><strong>Pockets</strong></h2>\n<p><strong>Reason for choice of subject</strong></p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; They are <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_31\">______</span> but can be overlooked by consumers and designers.</p>\n<p><strong>Pockets in men&rsquo;s clothes</strong></p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Men started to wear <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_32\">______</span> in the 18th century.</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; A <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_33\">______</span> sewed pockets into the lining of the garments.</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; The wearer could use the pockets for small items.</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Bigger pockets might be made for men who belonged to a certain type of <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_34\">______</span></p>\n<p><strong>Pockets in women&rsquo;s clothes</strong></p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Women&rsquo;s pockets were less <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_35\">______</span> than men&rsquo;s.</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Women were very concerned about pickpockets.</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Pockets were produced in pairs using <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_36\">______</span> to link them together.</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Pockets hung from the women&rsquo;s <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_37\">______</span> under skirts and petticoats.</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Items such as <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_38\">______</span> could be reached through a gap in the material.</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Pockets, of various sizes, stayed inside clothing for many decades.</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; When dresses changed shape, hidden pockets had a negative effect on the <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_39\">______</span> of women.</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Bags called &lsquo;pouches&rsquo; became popular, before women carried a <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_40\">______</span></p>",
